## 📋 Migration Notes

### Old Pattern (DEPRECATED - DO NOT USE)

```sql
-- ❌ Don't use pgcrypto
google_connector_ref BYTEA,
pgp_sym_encrypt(sqlc.narg(google_connector_ref), sqlc.arg(encryption_key))
pgp_sym_decrypt(google_connector_ref, sqlc.arg(encryption_key))
```

### New Pattern (Current - USE THIS)

```sql
-- ✅ Use TEXT and encrypt in repository
google_connector_ref TEXT,
google_connector_ref_hash VARCHAR(64),
-- Encryption handled in Go repository layer via encryptutils
```

## Summary

**Encryption Layer**: Database → Repository  
**Encryption Method**: pgcrypto → AES-GCM  
**Data Type**: BYTEA → TEXT  
**Key Management**: SQL parameter → Go repository struct  
**Benefits**: Better separation of concerns, easier testing, more flexible encryption
